---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import HeroHeader from "../../components/HeroHeader.astro";
import { createBreadcrumbSchema, createPageSchema, organizationSchema, site } from "../../data/site";

const pageDescription = "Northlight privacy policy: on-device compass, optional GPS altitude and speech, local preferences, and optional Pro purchases through Google Play.";
const effectiveDate = "15 October 2026";
const pagePath = "/privacy/northlight/";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Northlight Privacy Policy"
  description={pageDescription}
  canonicalPath={pagePath}
  structuredData={[
    organizationSchema,
    createPageSchema({
      type: "WebPage",
      name: "Northlight Privacy Policy",
      description: pageDescription,
      path: pagePath
    }),
    createBreadcrumbSchema([
      { name: "Home", path: "/" },
      { name: "Privacy", path: "/privacy/" },
      { name: "Northlight", path: pagePath }
    ])
  ]}
>
  <HeroHeader
    eyebrow="Northlight"
    title="Northlight Privacy Policy"
    tagline="On-device compass and light tools, optional GPS altitude and speech, and Pro purchases through Google Play."
  />

  <Breadcrumbs items={[
    { label: "Home", href: "/" },
    { label: "Privacy", href: "/privacy/" },
    { label: "Northlight" }
  ]} />

  <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="effective-date-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow" id="effective-date-heading">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
    <p>Northlight is a compass and lantern app made by Kreativ. Its compass and light tools are designed to work on your device.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="data-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h2 id="data-heading">Data we collect</h2>
    <p>Kreativ does not collect, sell, or share personal data through Northlight. The app has no account system, analytics, advertising SDKs, or developer-operated cloud services. Saved bearings, light-brightness preferences, speech speed and interval, the optional alignment-haptic preference, altitude units and whether a location permission request has been made, a cached Pro entitlement, and pending purchase-confirmation tokens are stored only on your device. Northlight does not save coordinates, routes, altitude history or audio recordings. These app records are excluded from Android cloud backup and device transfer.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="pro-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Google Play Billing</p>
    <h2 id="pro-heading">Optional Northlight Pro purchase</h2>
    <p>Northlight Pro is an optional one-time purchase processed by Google Play. The app uses internet access to communicate with Google Play Billing when it opens, when you buy or restore Pro, and when it retries purchase confirmation in the background. This checks ownership and confirms completed purchases; compass and light tools remain usable offline. Google handles payment under its own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>; Northlight does not receive or store payment-card details. Pending confirmation tokens are held locally by Android WorkManager for retries, and its completed-job records are subsequently pruned.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="permissions-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">On-device permissions</p>
    <h2 id="permissions-heading">Device permissions</h2>
    <p>Northlight requests camera permission only when you use its LED lantern, SOS signal, or Pro strobe. Android requires this permission to control the camera flash. Northlight never takes photos, records video, or accesses your media.</p>
    <p>The compass uses your device's orientation sensors locally to show magnetic north. Sensor readings do not leave your device.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="altimeter-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Optional location access</p>
    <h2 id="altimeter-heading">Optional GPS altimeter</h2>
    <p>The free altimeter requests precise foreground location only after you choose to enable it. Android supplies a GPS/GNSS location fix; Northlight uses its altitude, vertical uncertainty, timing and simulated-location flag to display a current altitude estimate. Northlight does not save the fix or coordinates, build a route, or send location or altitude to Kreativ or an elevation server. Only the current altitude estimate is held temporarily in memory. GPS measurement stops when you stop it, leave the home screen or lock the phone, and does not restart automatically. The app does not request background location. Compass, light and spoken-compass features work without location access. Android's own location services and device settings govern how the operating system obtains satellite fixes.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="speech-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Optional on-device audio</p>
    <h2 id="speech-heading">Optional spoken compass</h2>
    <p>Northlight sends a direction or accuracy warning to an installed Android text-to-speech engine using a voice marked as offline and installed, in the app's language. It does not send headings to a developer-operated speech service, use the microphone, or record audio. Speech stops when you leave the app. If a screen reader is active, an explicitly requested reading is handed to that accessibility service instead, which uses its own voice, connectivity and privacy settings. Choosing to manage or download voices opens external Android/voice-engine settings; voice downloads may use the internet and are governed by that provider.</p>
    <p>Pro owners can optionally request spoken phone-turn/alignment instructions for a saved magnetic bearing, with optional native alignment haptic feedback. This uses the same local speech path, not GPS or a routing service. Saved bearing names are not spoken; prompts use direction and degrees. Guidance pauses when you leave its screen or change/clear the target and never restarts automatically. The haptic preference is stored locally, and feedback respects Android settings and hardware availability. These cues describe phone orientation, not obstacle avoidance, safe routes or arrival at a place.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="links-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Only when selected</p>
    <h2 id="links-heading">External website links</h2>
    <p>The Made by Kreativ credit and privacy-policy link open a website in your browser only when you choose them. Northlight does not attach compass readings, altitude, saved bearings or purchase tokens to these links. Your browser and the destination website handle the visit under their own privacy settings and policies.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="children-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Children</p>
    <h2 id="children-heading">Children</h2>
    <p>Northlight does not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="changes-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Changes</p>
    <h2 id="changes-heading">Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be published on this page with a revised effective date.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
    <h2 id="contact-heading">Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions, contact <a class="cta" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
